From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Arun Iyengar <aiyengar1990@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 04 Nov 2026 18:00:00 +0000
Subject: media: cedrus: refuse interlaced MPEG-4 B-VOPs

In interlaced B-VOPs, the engine wraps the vertical component of the
forward, backward and bidirectional field motion vectors it decodes to
[-16 << (f_code - 1), 16 << (f_code - 1)), half the range of the f_code.
The ISO/IEC 14496-5 reference decoder and FFmpeg use the full range.
In vcon_ge_1_asp_l4, the engine reads a backward field vector of -33
(b_code 2) as 31. It is off in 36 to 298 macroblocks of each of the nine
B-VOPs, and in a B-VOP with both f_codes at 1, -17 wraps the same way.
So a narrower condition on f_code is not correct. Direct mode vectors
are not affected. No test stream has P-VOP field vectors past half the
range, so P-VOPs are left alone.

Fail such jobs instead of decoding them wrongly. Userspace should
decode streams that allow B-VOPs (low_delay is 0) in software.

Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Arun Iyengar <aiyengar1990@gmail.com>
---
--- a/drivers/staging/media/sunxi/cedrus/cedrus_mpeg4.c
+++ b/drivers/staging/media/sunxi/cedrus/cedrus_mpeg4.c
@@ -587,6 +587,17 @@
 		    vol->sprite_enable != V4L2_MPEG4_SPRITE_ENABLE_GMC)
 			return -EINVAL;
 
+		/*
+		 * In interlaced B-VOPs, the engine wraps the vertical component
+		 * of the field motion vectors it decodes to half the range that
+		 * the forward or backward f_code allows (the reference decoder
+		 * of ISO/IEC 14496-5 and FFmpeg use the full range), whatever
+		 * f_code is.
+		 */
+		if (coding_type == V4L2_MPEG4_VOP_CODING_TYPE_B &&
+		    (vol->flags & V4L2_MPEG4_VOL_FLAG_INTERLACED))
+			return -EINVAL;
+
 		/* Without the video packet positions, resync markers stop it. */
 		if (!run->mpeg4.num_slices &&
 		    !(vol->flags & V4L2_MPEG4_VOL_FLAG_RESYNC_MARKER_DISABLE))
